  "question": {
    "text": "White light reflected at normal incidence from a soap film has minima at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6500</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>∘</mo></mover></math> and maxima at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7500</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>∘</mo></mover></math> in the visible region without minimum in between. If <math><mi>μ</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> for the thin film, the thickness of the film is"
  },
